{"chunk_id": "da88baea8baf", "text": "This section of the Astika Parva describes the climax of King Janamejaya\u2019s snake\u2011sacrifice. The priests invoke powerful mantras to drag the serpent king Takshaka into the sacrificial fire, even though he has taken refuge with Indra. Indra appears in splendor, but when the ritual begins to pull Takshaka down from the heavens, he abandons the snake in fear. As Takshaka falls helplessly toward the flames, the young sage Astika intervenes and asks Janamejaya for a boon: that the sacrifice stop. The king, driven by vengeance, tries to offer wealth instead, but Astika refuses anything except the end of the slaughter to save his serpent relatives. The priests insist the king honor his promise. The narrative then begins listing the countless serpents already consumed by the fire, emphasizing the vast destruction caused by the ritual.\nDuring Janamejaya\u2019s snake sacrifice, Indra abandons Takshaka as mantras drag him toward the fire, but Astika asks the king to end the sacrifice.\nThemes: vengeance vs mercy, divine intervention, sacrifice ritual, boon and obligation, serpent lineage", "vector": [0.005405412521213293, -0.01730823889374733, -0.014455382712185383, 0.003873196430504322, -0.013841131702065468, 0.024419905617833138, -0.02620805986225605, 0.0014571407809853554, -0.007882893085479736, -0.011827751994132996, 0.00697175320237875, 4.11100554629229e-05, 0.02335520274937153, 0.031340472400188446, -0.01582038588821888, -0.006152751389890909, 0.052361518144607544, -0.002487718127667904, 0.015588335692882538, 0.0013658562675118446, -0.01931479386985302, 0.005541912745684385, 0.0066168527118861675, 0.026085209101438522, -0.014714733697474003, 0.015929587185382843, 0.00023951538605615497, -0.030139269307255745, 0.002102104714140296, -0.0021754736080765724, -0.0139435064047575, -0.0078965425491333, -0.004961786326020956, -0.003603608114644885, -0.032077573239803314, -0.00907727051526308, -0.002794843865558505, -0.0015714598121